---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout 
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  description="How The Driveway Mechanic handles product links and paid relationships."
  noIndex={true}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-foreground mb-8">Affiliate Disclosure</h1>
    
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
      <div class="not-prose mb-8 rounded-2xl border border-blue-500/20 bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-500/5 to-transparent p-6">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <div class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-white shrink-0">
            <svg class="h-6 w-6" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-400 mb-2">Product link information</h2>
            <p class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-300">
              The product links in our current guides are direct reference links without affiliate tracking added by this site. They lead to manufacturer information and coverage tools so you can check specifications and suitability before buying.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>When a paid relationship exists</h2>
      <p>
        If a link is part of an affiliate or other paid relationship, we will explain that we may receive a commission or other benefit when you use the link or make a purchase. We will place the disclosure with the related recommendation and link, using clear language.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Federal Trade Commission's <a href="https://www.ftc.gov/business-guidance/resources/ftcs-endorsement-guides-what-people-are-asking" class="text-accent hover:underline">endorsement guidance</a> explains disclosure of paid and other material relationships. It says disclosures should be clear and conspicuous and close to the recommendation.
      </p>

      <p>
        We do not claim that a product has been hands-on tested unless the article describes evidence for that testing. Product specifications and fitment should be checked against the manufacturer for the exact vehicle and product.
      </p>

      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/60 mt-8">
        <strong>Last updated:</strong> October 22, 2026
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
